  "estudio": "Chữ viết và phát âm 2",
  "alumno": "Writing and pronunciation (2): new letters and the other three tones"
 },
 "intro": "",
 "palabras": [],
 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "New consonants",
     "texto": [
      "**r**: in the north, a buzzing «z», as in «zoo»; in the south, a soft «r».",
      "**x**: like an «s».",
      "**c** and **k**: the same sound, a «k» without a puff of air, somewhere between «k» and «g». You write **k** before **i, e, ê, y**; in all other cases, **c**.",
      "**d** and **gi**: in the north, a buzzing «z»; in the south, like the «y» in «yes». (Careful: the **g** only sounds like this when it comes with **i**.)",
      "**th**: a «t» with a puff of air (like the English «t» in «teach»).",
      "**ch**: like the «ch» in «church».",
      "**kh**: like the «ch» in Scottish «loch», but softer."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "New vowels",
     "texto": [
      "**ơ**: a relaxed, neutral «e», with the mouth slightly open (like the English «o» in «other»).",
      "**ư**: a «u» with the lips spread, as if smiling. Only **c, t** or **-ng** can come after it.",
      "**ă**: like the Vietnamese «a», but short.",
      "**â**: a short **ơ**.",
      "**iê**: «ie», as in «ear». **ia**: «ia», as in «Maria».",
      "**ă, â** and **iê** never come without a final consonant."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The three tones that are left",
     "texto": [
      "**ạ · nặng** (dot below): as a first approximation in the north, it is usually short and low. ↓",
      "**ả · hỏi** (hook above): as a first approximation in the north, it usually falls and then rises again. ↘↗",
      "**ã · ngã** (tilde): in the north it usually includes tension or a break in the voice. The arrow does not show all of its features. ~↗",
      "In many southern varieties, **hỏi** and **ngã** are pronounced very similarly or have merged, although the writing keeps different marks. Pronunciation also varies within each region."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Repeat: r, x, c/k, d",
     "texto": [
      "Each row: **nặng · hỏi · ngã**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Repeat: the six tones in a row",
     "texto": [
      "You now have all six. Each row: **ngang · sắc · huyền · hỏi · ngã · nặng**. Don't worry about the meaning."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Same sound, different word",
     "texto": [
      "Change the tone or the vowel and the word changes. The most useful: **bạn** (friend), **bận** (busy) and **bán** (to sell)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
